sm:gap-4" style="opacity:0;transform:translateY(24px)"><div class="flex items-baseline gap-2 sm:w-[190px] sm:shrink-0"><span class="text-[13px] font-medium text-[#09090b]">Companies delivered</span><span class="text-[11px] tabular-nums text-[#a1a1aa]">47</span></div><div class="flex-1"><div class="h-7 w-full rounded-md bg-[#f4f4f5] overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full rounded-md transition-all bg-gradient-to-r from-[#FE7BCD] to-[#D64A9E]" style="width:12%"></div></div></div><div class="sm:w-[240px] sm:shrink-0"><span class="text-[11.5px] leading-snug text-[#71717a]">The only line you pay for. 5 credits each.</span></div></div></div></div></section><section id="intent" class="w-full bg-[#f4f2ef] border-y border-[#e4e4e7] py-16 md:py-24"><div class="max-w-[1180px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6"><p class="text-[11px] sm:text-xs font-medium tracking-[0.2em] uppercase text-[#09090b]/40 mb-6" style="opacity:0">[03] Intent, before you spend</p><h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl md:text-[38px] font-medium text-[#09090b] leading-[1.15] tracking-tight mb-4 max-w-[720px]" style="opacity:0;transform:translateY(24px)">A pricing-page visitor is worth finding. A blog bounce usually isn&#x27;t.</h2><p class="text-sm sm:text-[15px] text-[#71717a] leading-relaxed max-w-[620px] mb-10" style="opacity:0;transform:translateY(24px)">Point it at the pages that mean something - pricing, demo, security, a specific product page - and set a minimum number of pageviews. The filter runs before anything is resolved, so narrowing your intent narrows your bill too.</p><div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4"><div class="rounded-xl border border-[#e4e4e7] bg-white p-5" style="opacity:0;transform:translateY(24px)"><p class="text-[13px] font-medium text-[#09090b] mb-2">Everyone who read pricing twice</p><p class="text-[11.5px] text-[#a1a1aa] font-mono">/pricing, /plans · 2+ views</p></div><div class="rounded-xl border border-[#e4e4e7] bg-white p-5" style="opacity:0;transform:translateY(24px)"><p class="text-[13px] font-medium text-[#09090b] mb-2">Anyone who hit the demo page</p><p class="text-[11.5px] text-[#a1a1aa] font-mono">/demo · last 14 days</p></div><div class="rounded-xl border border-[#e4e4e7] bg-white p-5" style="opacity:0;transform:translateY(24px)"><p class="text-[13px] font-medium text-[#09090b] mb-2">Security reviewers</p><p class="text-[11.5px] text-[#a1a1aa] font-mono">/security, /trust · 1+ view</p></div></div></div></section><section class="w-full bg-white py-16 md:py-24"><div class="max-w-[1180px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6"><p class="text-[11px] sm:text-xs font-medium tracking-[0.2em] uppercase text-[#09090b]/40 mb-6" style="opacity:0">[04] What it will and won&#x27;t tell you</p><h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl md:text-[38px] font-medium text-[#09090b] leading-[1.15] tracking-tight mb-4 max-w-[760px]" style="opacity:0;transform:translateY(24px)">We could name a person for every visitor. It would be wrong, so we don&#x27;t.</h2><p class="text-sm sm:text-[15px] text-[#71717a] leading-relaxed max-w-[660px] mb-10" style="opacity:0;transform:translateY(24px)">We tested person-level visitor identification against known answers. Every vendor returned a confident name, and the names were wrong - shared office networks, VPN exits, and carrier NAT all look like one specific human to a resolver. So Origami stops at the company, where the claim holds up, and then finds the decision-maker there properly.</p><div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 lg:gap-10"><div class="rounded-xl border border-[#e4e4e7] bg-[#FAFAFA] p-6" style="opacity:0;transform:translateY(24px)"><p class="text-[13px] font-medium text-[#09090b] mb-4">What you get</p><ul class="space-y-3"><li class="flex items-start gap-2.5"><span class="mt-0.5 inline-flex h-4 w-4 items-center justify-center rounded-full shrink-0 bg-emerald-50 text-emerald-600"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-check h-2.5 w-2.5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg></span><span class="text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-[#71717a]">The <strong class="font-medium text-[#52525b]">company</strong> behind the visit, with the pages they read, how often, and when they were last on.</span></li><li class="flex items-start gap-2.5"><span class="mt-0.5 inline-flex h-4 w-4 items-center justify-center rounded-full shrink-0 bg-emerald-50 text-emerald-600"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-check h-2.5 w-2.5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg></span><span class="text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-[#71717a]">Only matches we&#x27;re confident in. Weak guesses are dropped rather than shipped and charged for.</span></li><li class="flex items-start gap-2.5"><span class="mt-0.5 inline-flex h-4 w-4 items-center justify-center rounded-full shrink-0 bg-emerald-50 text-emerald-600"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-check h-2.5 w-2.5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg></span><span class="text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-[#71717a]">Strangers only. Visitors who were signed in are your own signups, and your own team browsing from the office is filtered out too.</span></li></ul></div><div class="rounded-xl border border-[#e4e4e7] bg-[#FAFAFA] p-6" style="opacity:0;transform:translateY(24px)"><p class="text-[13px] font-medium text-[#09090b] mb-4">What we won&#x27;t claim</p><ul class="space-y-3"><li class="flex items-start gap-2.5"><span class="mt-0.5 inline-flex h-4 w-4 items-center justify-center rounded-full shrink-0 bg-[#f4f4f5] text-[#a1a1aa]"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-x h-2.5 w-2.5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M18 6 6 18"></path><path d="m6 6 12 12"></path></svg></span><span class="text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-[#71717a]">The individual person who visited. Nobody can do this reliably, whatever the category&#x27;s marketing says.</span></li><li class="flex items-start gap-2.5"><span class="mt-0.5 inline-flex h-4 w-4 items-center justify-center rounded-full shrink-0 bg-[#f4f4f5] text-[#a1a1aa]"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-x h-2.5 w-2.5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M18 6 6 18"></path><path d="m6 6 12 12"></path></svg></span><span class="text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-[#71717a]">Every visitor. About a quarter of genuine human traffic resolves to a named company, and coverage is best on business and office networks.</span></li><li class="flex items-start gap-2.5"><span class="mt-0.5 inline-flex h-4 w-4 items-center justify-center rounded-full shrink-0 bg-[#f4f4f5] text-[#a1a1aa]"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-x h-2.5 w-2.5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M18 6 6 18"></path><path d="m6 6 12 12"></path></svg></span><span class="text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-[#71717a]">Anyone else&#x27;s traffic. This reads your analytics and only yours.</span></li></ul></div></div><p class="mt-8 text-[12.5px] leading-relaxed text-[#a1a1aa] max-w-[660px]" style="opacity:0;transform:translateY(24px)">Visitor addresses are never stored or shown. They exist only inside the resolution step, and what we remember afterwards is the company, not the address it came from.</p></div></section><section class="w-full bg-[#f4f2ef] border-y border-[#e4e4e7] py-16 md:py-24"><div class="max-w-[1180px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6"><p class="text-[11px] sm:text-xs font-medium tracking-[0.2em] uppercase text-[#09090b]/40 mb-6" style="opacity:0">[05] Setup is one paste, not a deploy</p><h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl md:text-[38px] font-medium text-[#09090b] leading-[1.15] tracking-tight mb-4 max-w-[720px]" style="opacity:0;transform:translateY(24px)">Works through PostHog. No pixel, no script, no engineer.</h2><p class="text-sm sm:text-[15px] text-[#71717a] leading-relaxed max-w-[640px] mb-10" style="opacity:0;transform:translateY(24px)">PostHog is the one mainstream analytics tool that both keeps the raw visitor address and lets you authorize someone to read it. If you&#x27;re on it, this takes about a minute. If you&#x27;re on GA4, Plausible, Fathom, or Vercel, there is no address stored to resolve - we&#x27;d rather say that than sell you a table of nothing.</p><div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-5"><div class="rounded-xl border border-[#e4e4e7] bg-white p-6" style="opacity:0;transform:translateY(24px)"><span class="inline-flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-[#FEF0F7] mb-4"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-key-round h-4 w-4 text-[#D64A9E]" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2.586 17.414A2 2 0 0 0 2 18.828V21a1 1 0 0 0 1 1h3a1 1 0 0 0 1-1v-1a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h1a1 1 0 0 0 1-1v-1a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h.172a2 2 0 0 0 1.414-.586l.814-.814a6.5 6.5 0 1 0-4-4z"></path><circle cx="16.5" cy="7.5" r=".5" fill="currentColor"></circle></svg></span><p class="text-[13.5px] font-medium text-[#09090b] mb-1.5">Paste a read-only key</p><p class="text-[12.5px] leading-relaxed text-[#71717a]">Two scopes, both read-only: one to find the project, one to run the query. Nothing in Origami can write to your analytics.</p></div><div class="rounded-xl border border-[#e4e4e7] bg-white p-6" style="opacity:0;transform:translateY(24px)"><span class="inline-flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-[#FEF0F7] mb-4"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-shield-check h-4 w-4 text-[#D64A9E]" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 13c0 5-3.5 7.5-7.66 8.95a1 1 0 0 1-.67-.01C7.5 20.5 4 18 4 13V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1c2 0 4.5-1.2 6.24-2.72a1.17 1.17 0 0 1 1.52 0C14.51 3.81 17 5 19 5a1 1 0 0 1 1 1z"></path><path d="m9 12 2 2 4-4"></path></svg></span><p class="text-[13.5px] font-medium text-[#09090b] mb-1.5">Nothing touches your site</p><p class="text-[12.5px] leading-relaxed text-[#71717a]">No pixel, no script tag, no deploy. We read the traffic data you already collect, and you can revoke the key in PostHog at any time.</p></div><div class="rounded-xl border border-[#e4e4e7] bg-white p-6" style="opacity:0;transform:translateY(24px)"><span class="inline-flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-[#FEF0F7] mb-4"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-repeat h-4 w-4 text-[#D64A9E]" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m17 2 4 4-4 4"></path><path d="M3 11v-1a4 4 0 0 1 4-4h14"></path><path d="m7 22-4-4 4-4"></path><path d="M21 13v1a4 4 0 0 1-4 4H3"></path></svg></span><p class="text-[13.5px] font-medium text-[#09090b] mb-1.5">We check it actually works</p><p class="text-[12.5px] leading-relaxed text-[#71717a]">On connect we run a traffic probe and tell you the truth: live, no traffic yet, IP capture switched off, or a proxy collapsing every visitor onto one address.</p></div></div></div></section><section id="follow-through" class="w-full bg-white pt-16 pb-20 md:pt-20 md:pb-28"><div class="max-w-[1180px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6"><p class="text-[11px] sm:text-xs font-medium tracking-[0.2em] uppercase text-[#09090b]/40 mb-6" style="opacity:0">[06] A company name isn&#x27;t a pipeline</p><h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl md:text-[38px] font-medium text-[#09090b] leading-[1.15] tracking-tight mb-4 max-w-[720px]" style="opacity:0;transform:translateY(24px)">The list is the start. Origami does the rest in the same chat.</h2><p class="text-sm sm:text-[15px] text-[#71717a] leading-relaxed max-w-[620px] mb-12" style="opacity:0;transform:translateY(24px)">Every other tool in this category hands you a list of logos and calls it a product. A company row has nobody to email. Here it&#x27;s one continuous build.</p><div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-5"><div class="flex flex-col" style="opacity:0;transform:translateY(24px)"><span class="text-[11px] font-medium tracking-[0.2em] text-[#D64A9E] mb-3">01</span><p class="text-[14px] font-medium text-[#09090b] mb-2 leading-snug">Find the right person there</p><p class="text-[12.5px] leading-relaxed text-[#71717a]">A company row is a signal, not a contact. Origami runs a people search at each domain, filtered to the titles you actually sell to.</p></div><div class="flex flex-col" style="opacity:0;transform:translateY(24px)"><span class="text-[11px] font-medium tracking-[0.2em] text-[#D64A9E] mb-3">02</span><p class="text-[14px] font-medium text-[#09090b] mb-2 leading-snug">Get their contact details</p><p class="text-[12.5px] leading-relaxed text-[#71717a]">Verified work email, and a phone number if you work the phone. You are only charged when one is found.</p></div><div class="flex flex-col" style="opacity:0;transform:translateY(24px)"><span class="text-[11px] font-medium tracking-[0.2em] text-[#D64A9E] mb-3">03</span><p class="text-[14px] font-medium text-[#09090b] mb-2 leading-snug">Write from what they read</p><p class="text-[12.5px] leading-relaxed text-[#71717a]">The pages a company viewed are the best personalization material in outbound. An AI column reads them and drafts why they were probably looking.</p></div><div class="flex flex-col" style="opacity:0;transform:translateY(24px)"><span class="text-[11px] font-medium tracking-[0.2em] text-[#D64A9E] mb-3">04</span><p class="text-[14px] font-medium text-[#09090b] mb-2 leading-snug">Keep it topped up</p><p class="text-[12.5px] leading-relaxed text-[#71717a]">Visitors arrive continuously and every run picks up where the last one stopped, so the list refills itself daily instead of going stale.</p></div></div><div class="mt-12 rounded-xl border border-[#FECCE8] bg-gradient-to-br from-[#FEF0F7] via-white to-[#FEF0F7] p-6 sm:p-8" style="opacity:0;transform:translateY(24px)"><p class="text-[15px] font-medium text-[#09090b] mb-2">A one-off scan is the demo. The daily drip is the product.</p><p class="text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-[#71717a] max-w-[640px]">Each run resumes exactly where the last one stopped, so nobody is looked up - or paid for - twice. Leave it running and the companies reading your site this week are in your list by the time you sit down.</p></div></div></section></main><section class="py-20 md:py-28 bg-white w-full relative overflow-hidden"><div class="relative z-10 max-w-[1000px] mx-auto px-6 text-left"><h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl md:text-4xl font-medium tracking-[-0.5px] text-[#09090b] mb-4">Find your next perfect customers.</h2><p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-[#09090b]/50 mb-8 leading-relaxed max-w-xl">Join teams who are already using AI to build pipeline faster. Start your free trial today.</p><div class="flex items-center gap-2"><a href="/sign-up" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center h-9 px-4 text-sm font-medium text-[#D64A9E] bg-[#FEF0F7] border border-[#FE7BCD] hover:bg-[#FDDEED] hover:border-[#D64A9E] transition-all duration-150">Start Free</a><a href="https://calendly.com/d/cxyb-p4r-qwg" target="_blank" rel="noopener 